IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- vmu-time: the dates, periods and amounts that sections 1 to 12 of the Monetary Units Act 2004 (Victoria) state or imply.
-- This module imports only `prelude` and `daydate`, and uses no type of its own.
--
-- Units.
--   * A date is a DATE, written `Date day month year` (day first), which rolls an impossible date forward
--     (`Date 31 6 2024` is 1 July 2024), so every date here is built from a day that exists.
--   * An amount of money is a NUMBER of dollars, as the text writes "$".
--     The text names no other currency, and this module uses one.
--   * A rate is a NUMBER taken as a proportion: the text writes 2⋅5%, and `2.5%` is the number 0.025.
--     Where the text applies a rate as an increase (sections 5(6), 5(7), 9(1)(g)) the rate is added to 1.
--   * A financial year is named by the calendar year in which it commences on 1 July
--     (sections 6 and 11 say "the financial year commencing on 1 July").
--
-- Where the text does not answer, a function returns NOTHING (a MAYBE result) and a test says so.
-- "Nearest" is such a case: the text does not say which way an exact half goes, so a tie answers NOTHING.

§ `Section 2 -- commencement`

-- src:38 | (2) The remaining provisions of this Act come into operation on 1 July 2004.
@ref s 2(2) (src:38)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2(2) -- the day on which the remaining provisions come into operation` MEANS Date 1 7 2004

-- src:37 | (1) This section and sections 1, 3, 9, 11 and 12 come into operation on the day on which this Act receives the Royal Assent.
@ref s 2(1) (src:37)
GIVEN section IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) -- the section comes into operation on the day of the Royal Assent` MEANS
    elem section (LIST 1, 2, 3, 9, 11, 12)

-- The day of the Royal Assent is not stated in sections 1 to 12, so it is an input.
-- src:37 | (1) This section and sections 1, 3, 9, 11 and 12 come into operation on the day on which this Act receives the Royal Assent.
-- src:38 | (2) The remaining provisions of this Act come into operation on 1 July 2004.
@ref s 2(1), s 2(2) (src:37-38)
GIVEN section IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which this Act receives the Royal Assent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2 -- the day on which the section comes into operation` MEANS
    IF `s 2(1) -- the section comes into operation on the day of the Royal Assent` section
    THEN `the day on which this Act receives the Royal Assent`
    ELSE `s 2(2) -- the day on which the remaining provisions come into operation`

-- "come into operation on" a day: before that day the section has not come into operation, and from it the section has.
-- The text does not say how long a section stays in operation, so this says only that it has come into operation.
-- src:37 | (1) This section and sections 1, 3, 9, 11 and 12 come into operation on the day on which this Act receives the Royal Assent.
-- src:38 | (2) The remaining provisions of this Act come into operation on 1 July 2004.
@ref s 2(1), s 2(2) (src:37-38)
GIVEN section IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which this Act receives the Royal Assent` IS A DATE
      `the day asked about` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2 -- the section has come into operation by the day` MEANS
    `the day asked about` AT LEAST `s 2 -- the day on which the section comes into operation` section `the day on which this Act receives the Royal Assent`

§ `Sections 5, 6 and 11 -- the financial year`

-- The text says a financial year "commencing on 1 July" and speaks of "the previous financial year" and "the next financial year".
-- A financial year is named here by the calendar year in which it commences.
-- src:67 | Before 1 June in each year the Treasurer must publish in the Government Gazette and in a newspaper circulating generally throughout Victoria notice of—
-- src:68 | (a) the value of the fee unit that is to apply for the financial year commencing on 1 July in that year; and
@ref s 6 (src:67-68)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 6 -- the day on which the financial year commencing on 1 July in the year commences` MEANS Date 1 7 year

-- src:61 | (6) The amount of a fee unit fixed by the Treasurer that is to apply in respect of a financial year must not exceed the amount that is the product of the value of the fee unit in the previous financial year multiplied by the annual rate for the financial year in which the fee unit is to apply rounded to the nearest cent.
@ref s 5(6) (src:61)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 5(6) -- the year in which the previous financial year commences` MEANS year MINUS 1

§ `Section 5(4) -- the annual rate is fixed before 1 March`

-- src:59 | (4) The Treasurer is to fix before 1 March in each year an amount to be known as the annual rate by which the amount of a fee unit or penalty unit is to be adjusted for the next financial year.
@ref s 5(4) (src:59)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 5(4) -- the last day on which the annual rate for the financial year commencing on 1 July in the year may be fixed` MEANS
    Date (Day (Date 1 3 year) MINUS 1)

-- The text sets no earlier limit, so there is none here.
-- src:59 | (4) The Treasurer is to fix before 1 March in each year an amount to be known as the annual rate by which the amount of a fee unit or penalty unit is to be adjusted for the next financial year.
@ref s 5(4) (src:59)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which the annual rate is fixed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 5(4) -- the annual rate is fixed before 1 March in the year` MEANS
    `the day on which the annual rate is fixed` LESS THAN Date 1 3 year

§ `Section 6 -- notice before 1 June`

-- src:67 | Before 1 June in each year the Treasurer must publish in the Government Gazette and in a newspaper circulating generally throughout Victoria notice of—
@ref s 6 (src:67)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 6 -- the last day on which notice may be published in the year` MEANS
    Date (Day (Date 1 6 year) MINUS 1)

-- Notice must be published "in the Government Gazette and in a newspaper circulating generally throughout Victoria",
-- so both publications must fall before 1 June.
-- src:67 | Before 1 June in each year the Treasurer must publish in the Government Gazette and in a newspaper circulating generally throughout Victoria notice of—
@ref s 6 (src:67)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the day on which notice is published in the Government Gazette` IS A DATE
      `the day on which notice is published in a newspaper` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6 -- notice is published in the Gazette and in a newspaper before 1 June in the year` MEANS
        `the day on which notice is published in the Government Gazette` LESS THAN Date 1 6 year
    AND `the day on which notice is published in a newspaper` LESS THAN Date 1 6 year

§ `Section 9(2) -- 1 July 2004`

-- src:96 | (i) to take effect on or before 1 July 2004, the regulation converts fees in monetary amounts to fee units by dividing the amount of the fee by $10; or
@ref s 9(2)(a)(i) (src:96)
GIVETH A DATE
`s 9(2) -- 1 July 2004` MEANS Date 1 7 2004

-- src:96 | (i) to take effect on or before 1 July 2004, the regulation converts fees in monetary amounts to fee units by dividing the amount of the fee by $10; or
@ref s 9(2)(a)(i) (src:96)
GIVEN `the day on which the regulation takes effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(2) -- the regulation takes effect on or before 1 July 2004` MEANS
    `the day on which the regulation takes effect` AT MOST `s 9(2) -- 1 July 2004`

-- src:97 | (ii) to take effect after 1 July 2004, the regulation converts fees in monetary amounts to fee units by dividing the amount of the fee by the value of a fee unit fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3);
@ref s 9(2)(a)(ii) (src:97)
GIVEN `the day on which the regulation takes effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(2) -- the regulation takes effect after 1 July 2004` MEANS
    `the day on which the regulation takes effect` GREATER THAN `s 9(2) -- 1 July 2004`

§ `Section 11 -- the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012`

-- src:119 | (1) Despite sections 5 and 6, for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012—
@ref s 11(1) (src:119)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 11 -- the year in which the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012 commences` MEANS 2012

-- src:119 | (1) Despite sections 5 and 6, for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012—
@ref s 11(1) (src:119)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11 -- the financial year is the one commencing on 1 July 2012` MEANS
    year EQUALS `s 11 -- the year in which the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012 commences`

-- src:120 | (a) the value of a fee unit is $12.53; and
@ref s 11(1)(a) (src:120)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 11(1)(a) -- the value of a fee unit for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012, in dollars` MEANS 12.53

-- src:121 | (b) the value of a penalty unit is $140.84.
@ref s 11(1)(b) (src:121)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 11(1)(b) -- the value of a penalty unit for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012, in dollars` MEANS 140.84

-- src:123 | (3) Despite section 5, the annual rate for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012 is taken to be 2⋅5%.
@ref s 11(3) (src:123)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 11(3) -- the annual rate for the financial year commencing on 1 July 2012` MEANS 2.5%

§ `Rounding to the nearest`

-- "the nearest 10 cents" and "the nearest dollar" are the two roundings of section 7, and the same shape serves
-- "the nearest cent" of section 5(6) and (7): the multiple of the unit that is nearest to the amount.
-- The text does not say which way an exact half goes (for example 12.55 to the nearest 10 cents), so a tie answers NOTHING.
-- src:75 | (3) The amount of a fee calculated under this section may be rounded to the nearest 10 cents.
-- src:76 | (4) The amount of a penalty calculated under this section may be rounded to the nearest dollar.
@ref s 7(3), s 7(4) (src:75-76)
GIVEN amount IS A NUMBER
      unit IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the amount rounded to the nearest multiple of the unit` MEANS
    IF unit EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF (`the amount in units` MINUS FLOOR `the amount in units`) EQUALS 0.5
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST (unit TIMES FLOOR (`the amount in units` PLUS 0.5))
    WHERE
        `the amount in units` MEANS amount DIVIDED BY unit

§ `Section 4 and section 7 -- units to dollars`

-- src:53 | If in an Act, a statutory rule or a legislative instrument there is a statement of a number (whether whole, fractional or decimal) of what are called fee units, that statement must, unless the context otherwise requires, be construed as stating a number of dollars equal to the product obtained by multiplying the number of fee units by the amount fixed from time to time by the Treasurer under section 5(3).
@ref s 4 (src:53)
GIVEN `the number of fee units` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 4 -- the number of dollars a statement of fee units states` MEANS
    `the number of fee units` TIMES `the amount fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3)`

-- src:73 | (1) The amount of a fee provided for by an Act, a statutory rule or a legislative instrument by a fee unit is to be calculated by multiplying the number of fee units applicable by the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5.
@ref s 7(1) (src:73)
GIVEN `the number of fee units applicable` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 7(1) -- the amount of a fee, in dollars` MEANS
    `the number of fee units applicable` TIMES `the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5`

-- src:74 | (2) The amount of a penalty provided for by an Act or statutory rule by a penalty unit is to be calculated by multiplying the number of penalty units applicable by the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5.
@ref s 7(2) (src:74)
GIVEN `the number of penalty units applicable` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 7(2) -- the amount of a penalty, in dollars` MEANS
    `the number of penalty units applicable` TIMES `the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5`

-- src:75 | (3) The amount of a fee calculated under this section may be rounded to the nearest 10 cents.
@ref s 7(3) (src:75)
GIVEN `the amount of the fee calculated under section 7` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 7(3) -- the amount to which the fee may be rounded, to the nearest 10 cents` MEANS
    `the amount rounded to the nearest multiple of the unit` `the amount of the fee calculated under section 7` 0.1

-- src:76 | (4) The amount of a penalty calculated under this section may be rounded to the nearest dollar.
@ref s 7(4) (src:76)
GIVEN `the amount of the penalty calculated under section 7` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 7(4) -- the amount to which the penalty may be rounded, to the nearest dollar` MEANS
    `the amount rounded to the nearest multiple of the unit` `the amount of the penalty calculated under section 7` 1

§ `Section 5(6) and (7) -- the product, rounded to the nearest cent`

-- "the product of the value of the fee unit in the previous financial year multiplied by the annual rate ... rounded to the nearest cent".
-- The annual rate is a proportion (2⋅5% is 0.025), and the amount the subsection compares with is the previous value raised by it:
-- the previous value times one plus the annual rate; the rounding is of that product.
-- src:61 | (6) The amount of a fee unit fixed by the Treasurer that is to apply in respect of a financial year must not exceed the amount that is the product of the value of the fee unit in the previous financial year multiplied by the annual rate for the financial year in which the fee unit is to apply rounded to the nearest cent.
@ref s 5(6) (src:61)
GIVEN `the value of the fee unit in the previous financial year` IS A NUMBER
      `the annual rate for the financial year in which the fee unit is to apply` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 5(6) -- the product, rounded to the nearest cent` MEANS
    `the amount rounded to the nearest multiple of the unit`
        (`the value of the fee unit in the previous financial year` TIMES (1 PLUS `the annual rate for the financial year in which the fee unit is to apply`))
        0.01

-- src:62 | (7) The amount of a penalty unit fixed by the Treasurer that is to apply in respect of a financial year must not exceed the amount that is the product of the value of the penalty unit in the previous financial year multiplied by the annual rate for the financial year in which the penalty is to apply rounded to the nearest cent.
@ref s 5(7) (src:62)
GIVEN `the value of the penalty unit in the previous financial year` IS A NUMBER
      `the annual rate for the financial year in which the penalty is to apply` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 5(7) -- the product, rounded to the nearest cent` MEANS
    `the amount rounded to the nearest multiple of the unit`
        (`the value of the penalty unit in the previous financial year` TIMES (1 PLUS `the annual rate for the financial year in which the penalty is to apply`))
        0.01

§ `Section 9 -- conversion into units, and the roundings it deems`

-- src:96 | (i) to take effect on or before 1 July 2004, the regulation converts fees in monetary amounts to fee units by dividing the amount of the fee by $10; or
@ref s 9(2)(a)(i) (src:96)
GIVEN `the amount of the fee, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 9(2)(a)(i) -- the number of fee units when the fee is divided by 10 dollars` MEANS
    `the amount of the fee, in dollars` DIVIDED BY 10

-- src:97 | (ii) to take effect after 1 July 2004, the regulation converts fees in monetary amounts to fee units by dividing the amount of the fee by the value of a fee unit fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3);
@ref s 9(2)(a)(ii) (src:97)
GIVEN `the amount of the fee, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5(3)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 9(2)(a)(ii) -- the number of fee units when the fee is divided by the value of a fee unit` MEANS
    IF `the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5(3)` EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the amount of the fee, in dollars` DIVIDED BY `the value of a fee unit fixed under section 5(3)`)

-- src:99 | (i) to take effect on or before 1 July 2004, the regulation converts penalties in monetary amounts to penalty units by dividing the amount of the penalty by $100; or
@ref s 9(2)(b)(i) (src:99)
GIVEN `the amount of the penalty, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 9(2)(b)(i) -- the number of penalty units when the penalty is divided by 100 dollars` MEANS
    `the amount of the penalty, in dollars` DIVIDED BY 100

-- src:100 | (ii) to take effect after 1 July 2004, the regulation converts penalties in monetary amounts to penalty units by dividing the amount of the penalty by the value of a penalty unit fixed by the Treasurer under section 5(3);
@ref s 9(2)(b)(ii) (src:100)
GIVEN `the amount of the penalty, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5(3)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 9(2)(b)(ii) -- the number of penalty units when the penalty is divided by the value of a penalty unit` MEANS
    IF `the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5(3)` EQUALS 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST (`the amount of the penalty, in dollars` DIVIDED BY `the value of a penalty unit fixed under section 5(3)`)

-- "rounded up to the next 2 decimal places" is read as: rounded up to a multiple of 0.01, that is, to the smallest number
-- with at most 2 decimal places that is not less than the number calculated.
-- src:107 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2)(a) and (b), in calculating the number of fee units or penalty units, the number of fee units or penalty units is deemed to be calculated in accordance with those provisions if the fee unit or penalty unit is rounded up to the next 2 decimal places.
@ref s 9(3) (src:107)
GIVEN `the number of fee units or penalty units calculated` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 9(3) -- the number rounded up to the next 2 decimal places` MEANS
    (CEILING (`the number of fee units or penalty units calculated` TIMES 100)) DIVIDED BY 100

-- src:108 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (2)(f), in calculating the amount of a fee, the amount of the fee is deemed to be calculated in accordance with that provision if the fee is rounded to the nearest 10 cents.
@ref s 9(4) (src:108)
GIVEN `the amount of the fee calculated`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 9(4) -- the amount of the fee rounded to the nearest 10 cents` MEANS
    `the amount rounded to the nearest multiple of the unit` `the amount of the fee calculated` 0.1

-- src:109 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (2)(g), in calculating the amount of a penalty, the amount of the penalty is deemed to be calculated in accordance with that provision if the penalty is rounded to the nearest dollar.
@ref s 9(5) (src:109)
GIVEN `the amount of the penalty calculated` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 9(5) -- the amount of the penalty rounded to the nearest dollar` MEANS
    `the amount rounded to the nearest multiple of the unit` `the amount of the penalty calculated` 1

§ `Section 9(1)(g) and (2)(h) -- the cumulative annual rates`

-- "the cumulative annual rates fixed by the Treasurer ... for the period that the fee has had effect without any increase":
-- one annual rate for each financial year of the period, each applied to the amount that the year before left, so they compound.
-- With no year in the period the cumulative rate is 0.
-- src:93 | (g) increase any fees specified in monetary amounts in the statutory rule by the amount of the cumulative annual rates fixed by the Treasurer under this Act for the period that the fee has had effect without any increase.
@ref s 9(1)(g) (src:93)
GIVEN `the annual rates for the years of the period` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 9(1)(g) -- the cumulative annual rate` MEANS
    (product (map `one plus the rate` `the annual rates for the years of the period`)) MINUS 1
    WHERE
        `one plus the rate` rate MEANS 1 PLUS rate

-- src:93 | (g) increase any fees specified in monetary amounts in the statutory rule by the amount of the cumulative annual rates fixed by the Treasurer under this Act for the period that the fee has had effect without any increase.
@ref s 9(1)(g) (src:93)
GIVEN `the amount of the fee, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the annual rates for the years of the period` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 9(1)(g) -- the amount of the increase` MEANS
    `the amount of the fee, in dollars` TIMES `s 9(1)(g) -- the cumulative annual rate` `the annual rates for the years of the period`

-- src:106 | (h) in the case of a regulation made under subsection (1)(g), the regulation increases any fees that are less than the value of one fee unit by an amount not exceeding the cumulative annual rates fixed by the Treasurer under this Act for the period that the fee has had effect without any increase.
@ref s 9(2)(h) (src:106)
GIVEN `the amount of the fee, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the annual rates for the years of the period` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `the amount of the increase` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 9(2)(h) -- the increase does not exceed the cumulative annual rates` MEANS
    `the amount of the increase` AT MOST `s 9(1)(g) -- the amount of the increase` `the amount of the fee, in dollars` `the annual rates for the years of the period`
